course: dictionary
lesson: 10026
title: Tennis: a word in a sport
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A noun is a word for a thing, a person, a place or an activity. Tennis is a noun: it names a sport. When you meet a word like this, look at the words around it. «Tennis counts in a strange old way, love, 15, 30, 40, game» tells you that tennis has its own scoring.
explain: Look at the phrases tennis often belongs to: «play tennis», «tennis ball», «tennis racket», «tennis court». Each one shows what the other word is for. A tennis racket is what you hit the ball with, and a tennis court is the place where you play.
explain: Be careful with «table tennis». It is a different game, played on a table with small bats and a light ball. The word table in the phrase is a clue that this is not the game played on a court.
fact: Tennis is a sport for two or four players.
fact: In tennis, players hit a small ball over a net with rackets on a court.
fact: Tennis points go 0 (love), 15, 30, 40, then game.
fact: At 40-40 (deuce), you need two points in a row to win the game.
fact: Table tennis is a different game, played on a table with small bats and a light ball.
exercise: What is tennis? | A kind of pencil used in PE | A game played on a table with a light ball | *A sport for two or four players who hit a small ball over a net with rackets | A place where you buy rackets
exercise: «Tennis points go 0 (love), 15, 30, 40, game.» What does love mean in tennis? | Fifteen points | The game is over | *Zero, no points | A very good score
exercise: Which game is played on a table with small bats and a light ball? | A tennis racket | Tennis on a court | *Table tennis | Wimbledon
test: In the phrase «tennis court», what is the court? | The ball you hit | The name of a racket | The score | *The place where you play tennis
test: Why does the text say to keep a safe distance from someone swinging a tennis racket? | Because tennis is quiet | *Because a racket can hit your face | Because the ball is heavy | Because the net is high
exam: At 40-40 in tennis, what is the score called? | Game | Court | *Deuce | Love
